{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>And Jair son of Manasseh.</b> He is from the tribe of Judah, for so it is written that Hezron took the daughter of Machir son of Manasseh and begot from her Segub, and Segub begot Jair, who had the cities in the cities of Gilead. He is called after the family of his mother. There are also priests who were called after the sons of Barzillai the Gileadite, for so it is written. There is no place here to ask how Jair took an inheritance with another tribe, for it is the land of Canaan that is divided, not the land of the Amorite that is across the Jordan eastward, for there are Amorites in the land of Canaan. And he was the mightiest of the seven nations." "<b>Their villages.</b> Its meaning according to its context is like קריות (towns)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The comment appears to run two distinct arguments together without punctuation or connective; the syntax has been preserved as-is."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:20:12.461513067Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}